# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above each block.
@base = http://localhost:3000
@key = dev-key
# After creating an order, replace this with the orderNo from the response
@orderNo = ORD-0000000000000-000

### 1) Create an order (Idempotency-Key prevents duplicates; send it twice to see the replay)
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-001

{ "gameUid": "412000126173", "productCode": "DIAMOND_300", "amount": 138 }

### 2) Same key, different body -> 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-001

{ "gameUid": "412000126173", "productCode": "DIAMOND_300", "amount": 999 }

### 3) Look up one order
GET {{base}}/orders/{{orderNo}}

### 4) Bad format -> 400 INVALID_ORDER_NO
GET {{base}}/orders/ABC-123

### 5) Unknown order -> 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND
GET {{base}}/orders/ORD-1111111111111-111

### 6) List: current / history, newest first, paginated
GET {{base}}/orders?tab=current&page=1&pageSize=10

###
GET {{base}}/orders?tab=history&page=1

### 7) Timeline
GET {{base}}/orders/{{orderNo}}/timeline

### 8) Customer reports a problem
POST {{base}}/orders/{{orderNo}}/report-issue
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "ITEM_NOT_RECEIVED", "detail": "paid 10 minutes ago" }

### 9) Bank webhook: needs an HMAC signature, so run this in a terminal instead:
#    npm run pay -- ORD-xxxxxxxxxxxxx-xxx            (add a 2nd arg to reuse an event id)

### 10) Bot claims the next paid order (204 when the queue is empty)
POST {{base}}/bot/claim
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{key}}

{ "botId": "bot-1" }

### 11) Bot heartbeat (extends the lease)
POST {{base}}/bot/orders/{{orderNo}}/heartbeat
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{key}}

{ "botId": "bot-1" }

### 12a) Bot completes the top-up
POST {{base}}/bot/orders/{{orderNo}}/complete
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{key}}

{ "botId": "bot-1", "providerRef": "TX-123" }

### 12b) ...or reports failure. retryable=false (wrong UID) -> FAILED, true -> backoff retry
POST {{base}}/bot/orders/{{orderNo}}/fail
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{key}}

{ "botId": "bot-1", "reason": "UID not found", "retryable": false }

### 13) Support fixes the UID and re-queues
POST {{base}}/admin/orders/{{orderNo}}/fix-uid
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{key}}

{ "gameUid": "412000126174" }

### 14) Support refunds a FAILED / DELAYED order
POST {{base}}/admin/orders/{{orderNo}}/refund
X-Api-Key: {{key}}

### 15) Run the scheduler once by hand (it also runs every 30s)
POST {{base}}/admin/sweep
X-Api-Key: {{key}}
